# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: through a header declaring nothing and writing `#pragma clang
# diagnostic ignored "-Wimplicit-function-declaration"`, `getpid() -> i64`
# built with no warning at all and printed `true`, C calling a function no
# header declares, its result read as the `int` C assumes (panel 205's
# `ifd`; with a parameter, `getpid(x: f64)`, the base already refused it).
#
# CAUSE: clang makes an implicit declaration an error by default in C99 and
# after, and the header's pragma turned it off.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-an-undeclared-function-is-refused-through-the-pragma.h"
    function getpid() -> i64  #~ ffi_unknown_name

function main()
    print(getpid() > 0)
